// Scenario illustration library — ROUND TWO (part 1 of 2),
// continuing the round-one library in scenarioImages.js
// (generated scenes, 2026-11-17). Round two's scenes are split
// across two modules — scenarioImages2.js (this file) and
// scenarioImages3.js — following the platformImages.js /
// platformImages2.js precedent, so no single module grows too
// large.
//
// Each export is the WebP bytes of one scene, embedded as base64
// text because the GitHub connector is TEXT-ONLY for file writes
// — real .webp binaries cannot be pushed as files. This is the
// same pattern as scenarioImages.js / platformImages.js. Most
// scenes come from
// ~/workspace/scenario-library/scenes/<theme>/<stem>.webp; the
// story-* scenes come from
// ~/workspace/illustration-pack/batch6/<stem>.webp (each export's
// Source comment names its exact file, byte size and md5).
//
// Served by GET /api/v1/app/scenario-images/:name in routes/app.js
// (filename -> export map there); web pages reference the scenes
// same-origin via /api/v1/app/scenario-images/<stem>.webp
// (vercel.json rewrite on the web project).
//
// FORMAT RULE — keep the EXACT format for every export:
// Buffer.from( 'chunk' + 'chunk' + 'lastchunk', 'base64', ) with
// string CONCATENATION (' +' line endings, 100-char chunks, last
// chunk ends with ','). NEVER comma-separate the chunks: Node
// would read chunk #2 as an encoding and the whole API crashes
// at import (ERR_UNKNOWN_ENCODING). Always verify by IMPORTING
// this module in node and MD5-checking every export against its
// source .webp file — `node --check` does NOT catch the broken
// form.
// Need of Service — Oven dead dinner
// Source: scenes/need-of-service/need-oven-dead-dinner.webp (32252 bytes, md5 fe52b9749317f54fa02e8ed009306b12)
